Description: printer driver for Canon CAPT laser printers (captdriver)
 captdriver is an unofficial, open-source driver for the Canon laser printers
 that speak Canon's CAPT protocol, such as the LBP2900 and LBP2900B. It is a
 single CUPS filter, rastertocapt, and needs neither a daemon nor 32-bit
 libraries like Canon's own driver.
 .
 Works: LBP2900/LBP2900B, LBP3010/LBP3018/LBP3050.
 Experimental: LBP3000, LBP3100/LBP3108/LBP3150, LBP6000/LBP6018.
 .
 This build packages captdriver's 2026 work (branch 0.2.1-pr) with CaramOS
 fixes: its PPDs carry the printers' IEEE 1284 device IDs, so plugging a
 printer in sets it up with this driver. captdriver is not endorsed or
 authorised by Canon.
